40e47178c6bf9b25884639d16c50b4062b365b7c31ea4c5e42b20bd91c79c0f","speaker":"Dave","turn_index":27},{"dia_id":"D25:28","global_turn_index":452,"locator":"[S25T28]","raw_turn_sha256":"3a979df11fa97574e4ad288e6ef0fbd8d8add6c4e571063f8ac122c48e39544b","rendered_turn_sha256":"d13471547df9dbbab2350f3298387b0b747a9ee23c8c70d0f14b276cc76f95a2","session_date":"2023-10-23","session_datetime":"2023-10-23T14:17:00","session_id":"session_25","session_index":25,"source_sha256":"30da8ac057b5ba2a01d708f338f32ec49f3e1d5136e794ae31ac6e0469a0322f","speaker":"Calvin","turn_index":28},{"dia_id":"D25:29","global_turn_index":453,"locator":"[S25T29]","raw_turn_sha256":"6396f39a92129b6b07aaff5cd11a2585c43ebebf31407b7113f75649534d3b10","rendered_turn_sha256":"2ee065d79c9c9c44873e7c05c27609ee73a189e7ef7e47a21ec5494e7d3ce811","session_date":"2023-10-23","session_datetime":"2023-10-23T14:17:00","session_id":"session_25","session_index":25,"source_sha256":"9819faaa9e3daea1d7ccd294aa39a98fc292ce15e4ebcf55f1858821f48f96ab","speaker":"Dave","turn_index":29},{"dia_id":"D25:30","global_turn_index":454,"locator":"[S25T30]","raw_turn_sha256":"942960fcc5f77d583520421934d10d4fb6108d3ea7d6cb880f0138ef541980f7","rendered_turn_sha256":"1daef6433be067ccca85cc092abd16e4b631252ac40f2a8632fa4d64fc376207","session_date":"2023-10-23","session_datetime":"2023-10-23T14:17:00","session_id":"session_25","session_index":25,"source_sha256":"8d64408ad12c4ed4cfa279f0b788d3c785331c4e97486afee7ccc31bbb354965","speaker":"Calvin","turn_index":30},{"dia_id":"D25:31","global_turn_index":455,"locator":"[S25T31]","raw_turn_sha256":"df03ad4bbd97ec36c5aa8149a4bc939b4c468d73716e5c29e44077e29835d8c4","rendered_turn_sha256":"db25c21dcb83a78011fc015dd4aff2ffe21f91637662017671c6824b1ea3a502","session_date":"2023-10-23","session_datetime":"2023-10-23T14:17:00","session_id":"session_25","session_index":25,"source_sha256":"d5b527d2a3b937c66821ee2458a2f878f485df2636ce4b0d491a837c247b9f11","speaker":"Dave","turn_index":31}],"speaker":null,"store_id":"s3","store_snapshot_sha256":"983238fddc77a88ef4ae3d06b50bcfd25a429f497e89c6af4d9477cefca9cad2","text":"- On 2023-10-23, caught up with Dave about the tour and fame: Dave opened by asking how the tour with Frank Ocean is going, noting he'd been \"pondering our chat the other day about fame and its impact on relationships\" (a chat not otherwise recorded in this memory) — \"It must be awesome but it must have its own struggles too\" — and how Calvin is juggling his job plus his personal life; Calvin: the tour's been incredible — performing and connecting with the crowd has been so energizing — but fame has its own challenges and it's been tough trying to balance everything [S25T1][S25T2]. Dave asked how he's managing and whether he ever feels overwhelmed; Calvin: he takes it one day at a time, but it can get overwhelming with so many demands — still, he enjoys what he does so he pushes on [S25T3][S25T4]. Dave asked for strategies, and Calvin: a strong support system is really helpful — his friends and team keep him on track [S25T5][S25T6]. Dave then shared that he recently had a good conversation with some neighbors about current events and politics — it was nice to hear different perspectives and share their own, and interacting like that cheers him up and helps him stay informed — and asked Calvin the same (Dave's side in the Relationships section of /memories/dave.md); Calvin: staying connected and up-to-date on world events is important to him — it helps his music stand out by incorporating unique perspectives, connects him better with his fans, and keeps him motivated and inspired [S25T7][S25T8]. The conversation then turned to art (Dave: \"Art is amazing how it reflects the world\"): asked whether anything caught Calvin's eye lately and impacted his music; Calvin: yes — recently he's been really inspired by the struggles that people go through, which has made him dig deeper into his music to try to capture those feelings [S25T9][S25T10]. Dave asked whether using his music to share experiences and feelings is cathartic for him; Calvin: yes — it's a way for him to express himself and work through his emotions — \"like my own form of therapy\" [S25T11][S25T12]. Dave agreed (\"I get it\"), saying cars give him an outlet to express himself — \"like a little oasis of calm\" — that working on a car is \"like I'm connecting back with myself,\" and that the music helps too; he shared a photo of his garage (a little dirty, but everything in its place, tools hanging on the wall) [S25T13]. Calvin: \"Looking cool — what made you start working on cars?\"; Dave: ever since he was ten he's been fascinated with how machines work — he found an old car in a neighbor's garage, asked if he could fix it, and that's when his love for car engineering began — he enjoyed transforming it from broken-down to high-running, and that sense of accomplishment hooked him, so he's been working on cars ever since (shared a photo of a man working on a car in a garage) [S25T14][S25T15]. Calvin: \"Impressive! That must have taken a lot of skill and determination to bring that car back to life,\" and asked whether it was a classic car and whether Dave still has it or is currently working on another project [S25T16]; Dave answered in the continuation of the chat: \"Thanks Calvin! It was a fun project. I restored a car last year, but I sold it to a collector\" (Dave's 2022 restoration — details in the Classic cars section of /memories/dave.md), and he's \"now working on something new, and it's quite a challenge!\" — sharing a photo of his new project car (a black car parked in a parking lot — \"Take a look at this wonderful car!\") [S25T17]. Calvin: \"Cool! Been wanting to try that. What would you say is the toughest part of car restoration?\" — Dave: it takes a lot of patience but the payoff is worth it, and paying extra attention to detail isn't easy but it pays off (details in the Hobbies and sense of purpose section of /memories/dave.md) [S25T18][S25T19]. Calvin: details \"can really make a difference\" and are what makes something great — \"like a well-crafted rap song or a sleek and stylish car\" [S25T20]; Dave: paying attention to details \"makes a big difference, whether it's in music or with vehicles\" — little things can make a big impact [S25T21]. Calvin: without those details it's just average, and as an artist he wants to create something extraordinary — sharing a photo of his record (a silver disc in a black frame on a table; his side in the Music section of this file) [S25T22]; Dave: he loves the attention to detail in Calvin's work — \"it makes it extra special. Keep on creating!\" — sharing a photo of his brown amp (a brown amp with a black knob and a brown cover; Dave's side in the Music section of /memories/dave.md) [S25T23]; Calvin: \"Thanks Dave! Appreciate your support!\" [S25T24]. The chat then turned to concerts: Dave, glad that Calvin liked his garage, said the good times he's had at concerts last month (~September 2023) remind him that \"music has a way of connecting us and making memories\" — \"Take a look at this picture, the atmosphere was amazing!\" (shared a photo of a crowd of people at a concert with their hands in the air); Calvin: \"Music has a way of bringing us together and creating unforgettable memories. It's unbeatable in terms of the energy it brings\" (shared a photo of a crowd of people at a concert with their hands in the air); Dave: \"Concerts are awesome, they bring people together and create such a cool vibe. You can feel the energy in the air.\" — sharing another photo from a concert (a crowd of people standing around a stage — \"this unforgettable moment that I captured\"); Calvin: \"Concerts are what I live for - the indescribable connection between the artist and the crowd is just amazing!\" [S25T25][S25T26][S25T27][S25T28]; Dave: \"Wow, it's amazing how that connection between artist and crowd can be indescribable. So glad you get to experience that!\" [S25T29]; 